          "semantic_formula_digest": "sha256:f09a9d282be02c94c77576bbe039723582a985d0668153121ce393c96dceb5b9",
          "purpose": "author_intent_academic",
          "latex": "\\mathbf{q} \\cdot \\mathbf{p}_i",
          "prose_explanation": "The core mechanism is the dot-product similarity computation between a static query vector and contextualized passage vectors, followed by a descending sort. This aligns with the author's intent to avoid full-text processing and autoregressive generation.",
          "markdown_block": "### Inference Scoring and Ranking\n\nThe inference procedure realizes the ranking mechanism by computing the relevance score for each candidate passage $i$ as the dot product between the unchanged query embedding $\\mathbf{q} \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$ and the contextualized passage embedding $\\mathbf{p}_i \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$:\n\n$$\ns_i = \\mathbf{q} \\cdot \\mathbf{p}_i = \\sum_{k=1}^{d} q_k p_{i,k}\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the embedding dimensionality. The system then sorts the passages in descending order of $s_i$ to produce the final ranking. This operation avoids autoregressive generation, thereby reducing inference latency. The assumption is that the query embedding $\\mathbf{q}$ remains static during the inference phase, while the passage embeddings $\\mathbf{p}_i$ are contextualized based on the input context.",
          "symbol_definitions": [],
